"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. Initially allocated a budget of $500,000 for phase one, the budget was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. The project has reached significant milestones, including the successful completion of the testing phase and ahead-of-schedule prototype testing for secure file sharing. A celebration for this milestone is planned for October 10th. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October. Additionally, the executive board has approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing, with detailed allocations to be discussed on August 1st. Specific sub-budgets include $55,000 for compliance (including training and audits) and $15,000 for specialized training for coding teams and project managers. The team is also exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Onboarding for the Zenith Innovations team is scheduled for April 15th, 2023."
